    <h2 class="h2" style="margin-bottom:18px">What are LED and LCD Video Walls?</h2>
    <p>A video wall is a single large canvas built from LED cabinets or bezel-thin LCD panels, driven by a processor that decides what appears where. Pixel pitch, viewing distance and content resolution have to be decided together, before anyone quotes a number.</p>
    <h3>How video wall design works</h3>
    <table class="deftable"><tbody><tr><th>Content and resolution</th><td>We start from the content you will actually show and the resolution it exists in.</td></tr><tr><th>Viewing distance</th><td>Pixel pitch is calculated from the closest viewer, so the image is neither pixelated nor needlessly expensive.</td></tr><tr><th>Wall geometry</th><td>Overall size and aspect ratio are set by sightlines and the architecture.</td></tr><tr><th>Processing</th><td>Inputs, outputs, window layouts and presets are specified with headroom for future sources.</td></tr><tr><th>Structure and power</th><td>Mounting, service access, power and cooling are engineered with your contractors.</td></tr><tr><th>Commissioning and service</th><td>Calibration, alignment, spare modules and a maintenance plan at handover.</td></tr></tbody></table>
    <h3>Key features that define an effective system</h3>
    <table class="deftable"><tbody><tr><th>Correct pixel pitch</th><td>Calculated, not guessed, from real viewing distances.</td></tr><tr><th>Seamless canvas</th><td>LED with no bezels, or LCD with sub-millimetre joins.</td></tr><tr><th>Calibrated uniformity</th><td>Brightness and colour matched cabinet to cabinet.</td></tr><tr><th>Flexible windowing</th><td>Multiple sources, sizes and presets on the same wall.</td></tr><tr><th>Serviceable design</th><td>Front or rear access planned before fabrication.</td></tr><tr><th>Redundancy options</th><td>Backup processing and power where downtime is unacceptable.</td></tr></tbody></table>
